cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the deposit below, the thesis, and the article in the references."
title: "Melanoma under CAR T-cell therapy with TAM-mediated immunosuppression: model analysis, Bayesian calibration and identifiability (code and data)"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Rodrigues
    given-names: Guilherme
    affiliation: "São Paulo State University (UNESP), Institute of Biosciences, Botucatu"
abstract: >-
  Code and data of Chapter 3 of the doctoral thesis: a three-population ordinary differential equation
  model of cutaneous melanoma under CAR T-cell therapy with tumor-associated macrophages, its equilibria
  and local stability, the Hopf bifurcation driven by the pro-tumoral action of the macrophages, a
  variance-based global sensitivity analysis, the Bayesian calibration against the immunocompetent B16
  data of Jilani et al. (2024), the structural and practical identifiability analyses, and the
  computational scenarios built on them.
keywords:
  - mathematical oncology
  - CAR T-cell therapy
  - melanoma
  - tumor-associated macrophages
  - Bayesian calibration
  - parameter identifiability
  - Hopf bifurcation
  - global sensitivity analysis
